  "id": "oral-method",
  "term": "oral method",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, the oral method is an approach to educating deaf people that teaches speech by having them imitate the visible movements of the lips and voice in speaking, while also training them to understand others by watching lip movements. When used together with the manual alphabet, it was called the combined method.",
